Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraRadarCoordinates", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"fccb5d1b-cbc8-4159-ba22-001ee2e8fd21"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraRadarCoordinates"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraRadarCoordinates", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5a1eef92-d863-4670-8556-47654a3ce5ce"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the radar coordinates of the observer ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ": every event between the first and the last tick of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " gets its radar time and radar distance.",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"d5d430ba-1241-4af3-9faa-211165c17b3e"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraRadarCoordinates"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraRadarCoordinates", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", " ", 
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], ",", " ", "\[Ellipsis]"}], "}"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5cdbdd81-d7d4-4f43-a782-67f445e4f269"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "joins the radar coordinates of several observers on the events they all \
chart."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"4167ad13-004c-4df6-adea-245780fe8773"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: for an observer ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " = (",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 "1 \[Precedes] ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 "2 \[Precedes] \[Ellipsis] \[Precedes] ",
 StyleBox["ak", "TI"],
 "), a chain given as a vertex list in causal order, and an event ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 " of the radar domain [",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 "1, ",
 StyleBox["ak", "TI"],
 "], the emission tick is ",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 ") = max{",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 " : ",
 StyleBox["ai", "TI"],
 " \[PrecedesSlantEqual] ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 "}, the latest tick that can signal ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 ", and the reception tick is ",
 StyleBox["j", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 ") = min{",
 StyleBox["j", "TI"],
 " : ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 " \[PrecedesSlantEqual] ",
 StyleBox["aj", "TI"],
 "}, the earliest tick ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 " can signal. The radar time of ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 " is (",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 " + ",
 StyleBox["j", "TI"],
 ")/2 and its radar distance (",
 StyleBox["j", "TI"],
 " \[Minus] ",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 ")/2."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1592c72b-b08f-4c67-a33e-23d15d904d2a"],

Cell["\<\
This is the radar construction of special relativity, made with the ticks of \
a clock instead of the readings of a continuous one: an event on the observer \
is its own emission and reception, at distance 0 and at its own tick; an \
event off it is seen by the latest signal that can reach it and answers the \
earliest signal it can send. Radar time is weakly monotone along every edge \
and radar distance is never negative. Radar distance is unsigned, so a single \
observer cannot tell left from right: the chart of a symmetric observer folds \
the graph along it. Joining the charts of several observers separates what \
one of them identifies.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6d31b888-c805-4908-a5a7-ef297b08e618"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The head holds its observers and computes nothing. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3e601dd7-7cc8-495f-bdb1-28234e2efa9c"],
 " reads it on a graph:"
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"63a6bf32-192e-4ff0-a15b-e3f9a2a7ef36"],

